WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.233 --> 00:00:04.003
-What you do is important.

00:00:04.003 --> 00:00:07.407
Meanwhile, all I do is invent
little people in my head

00:00:07.407 --> 00:00:10.743
and make them have imaginary
conversations with each other.

00:00:10.743 --> 00:00:13.345
-Books change people's lives.

00:00:13.345 --> 00:00:15.748
-Has something I've written
ever changed your life?

00:00:15.748 --> 00:00:17.917
-Absolutely.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.553
Absolutely.

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:23.189
My dining room table
was wobbly as hell...

00:00:23.189 --> 00:00:24.290
-Oh, my God.

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:25.424
-...until your last book
came out.

00:00:25.424 --> 00:00:27.326
It was like, perfect.

00:00:27.326 --> 00:00:29.028
I'm telling you --
-Take me back to Logan, please.

00:00:29.028 --> 00:00:30.697
-Logan cannot help you, Monk.

00:00:30.697 --> 00:00:32.532
-Oh, my God.

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:33.666
-Welcome back to "Late Night."

00:00:33.666 --> 00:00:36.069
We're here
with Tracee Ellis Ross!

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:38.571
That was a clip
from "American Fiction."

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.706
Now, I was not familiar
with the book.

00:00:40.706 --> 00:00:43.743
It's "Erasure" that
it's based on, which is 2001?

00:00:43.743 --> 00:00:45.111
-I'm not sure.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.079
I'm actually grateful
I had not read the book,

00:00:47.079 --> 00:00:49.248
because it let me come
to the script really clean.

00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:50.883
-That's probably
a nice feeling, right?

00:00:50.883 --> 00:00:52.718
I think sometimes, when there's
books that you're familiar with,

00:00:52.718 --> 00:00:53.853
it's very hard to
step into the role.

00:00:53.853 --> 00:00:55.421
-Yeah, Percival --

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:56.856
It's an extraordinary book.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:59.459
I still have not read it.
That's problematic.

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.360
Bad student.

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.661
But it's a great movie.

00:01:02.661 --> 00:01:04.163
I got to work
with Jeffrey Wright,

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:06.132
beautiful ensemble cast,
Issa Rae,

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:08.901
Sterling K. Brown,
Leslie Uggams.

00:01:08.901 --> 00:01:12.338
And it's a story about a man
who's trying to make sense

00:01:12.338 --> 00:01:15.074
of who he is in the world versus
how the world sees him.

00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:17.377
And then it's really funny
with a lot of --

00:01:17.377 --> 00:01:20.212
I don't know, I'm so honored
and proud to be in this movie.

00:01:20.212 --> 00:01:21.180
-I've heard great things,

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:22.848
and I really love
Jeffrey Wright,

00:01:22.848 --> 00:01:25.351
and I've been lucky enough
to have him here a few times.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:26.486
And, you know,
obviously, he's acting,

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:27.887
but he laughs at you
in the clip.

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:30.557
I will say, in real life...
-Yes.

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:31.824
-...getting Jeffrey Wright
to laugh at you

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.359
feels like a huge compliment.

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:35.361
-Listen, Eddie Murphy
laughing at you is one thing.

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:36.462
-Yeah.
-Because the man laughs,

00:01:36.462 --> 00:01:37.529
you know what I mean?

00:01:37.529 --> 00:01:38.831
-He's a laugher.
-He's a laugher.

00:01:38.831 --> 00:01:40.200
Jeffrey Wright...

00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.701
So he broke when we were --

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.836
we were shooting
the first couple of takes,

00:01:43.836 --> 00:01:46.005
and you know, it was in a car,

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:48.640
so the director wasn't
in there to say "cut,"

00:01:48.640 --> 00:01:50.076
so I had time to just go.

00:01:50.076 --> 00:01:51.277
So I was just improvving
and talking, whatever.

00:01:51.277 --> 00:01:52.545
And all of a sudden,
Jeffrey starts laughing.

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:54.046
I was like,
"What are you laughing at?"

00:01:54.046 --> 00:01:55.381
And he's like, "You."

00:01:55.381 --> 00:01:56.482
And I was like, "What?"
He's like, "You're funny."

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.751
I'm like,
"I know. We're acting!

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.286
What are you doing,
Jeffrey Wright, huh?"

00:02:01.286 --> 00:02:02.855
And then I was like, "Oh,
my God, I can make him laugh.

00:02:02.855 --> 00:02:04.157
I'm going to keep going."

00:02:04.157 --> 00:02:06.125
-It was so much fun.
-I do not blame you at all.

00:02:06.125 --> 00:02:07.260
-Oh, it was fantastic.

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:09.195
What an actor he is.
-He's the best.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.396
He is the best.
-[ Gasps ] Oh, my Lord.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:11.630
-But I'm going to say this.

00:02:11.630 --> 00:02:13.600
You got an Eddie Murphy project.
-I can't.

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:15.701
-Jeffrey Wright project.
-Stop. Stop it.

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:17.637
-But you turned up in a movie

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:18.938
that might be
the biggest one of all.

00:02:18.938 --> 00:02:22.241
-Let me tell you something.
I'm gonna be famous.

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:23.409
You guys...

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:24.743
-Did you know
this one was coming?

00:02:24.743 --> 00:02:25.711
-No!
-Because this one --

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:27.580
-Alright, so you are in...

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:28.614
-You guys don't even know
what it is.

00:02:28.614 --> 00:02:29.882
Just get excited, alright?

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.585
-This is so exciting.
Tracee was in a movie

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:33.920
that she didn't know
she was going to be in,

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:35.655
and that movie was
Beyonce's "Renaissance."

00:02:35.655 --> 00:02:36.990
-What?

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:39.125
[ Applause ]

00:02:39.125 --> 00:02:42.328
-Yeah, I have a guest appearance

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:44.263
in the
Beyonce "Renaissance" movie.

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:46.966
And yes, it's during
the mute challenge.

00:02:46.966 --> 00:02:48.401
-So it was during
the mute challenge and you --

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.468
We're going to show the clip.

00:02:49.468 --> 00:02:51.237
You seem very proud of yourself

00:02:51.237 --> 00:02:52.905
for how you execute
the mute challenge.

00:02:52.905 --> 00:02:54.440
-It's very embarrassing.
-It's very --

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:55.842
-It's not great.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.944
So the mute challenge,
people know the mute challenge,

00:02:57.944 --> 00:03:00.013
and I figured I really
didn't want to mess it up,

00:03:00.013 --> 00:03:02.882
so I was just quiet
for most of the song.

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:05.818
-Let's take a look at
Tracee's wonderful cameo

00:03:05.818 --> 00:03:07.052
in "Renaissance."

00:03:07.052 --> 00:03:08.054
-I'm ready, I'm ready!

00:03:08.054 --> 00:03:08.955
-♪ Everybody on mute ♪

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:13.526
[ Crowd quiets ]

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:15.394
♪ Look around,
it's me and my crew ♪

00:03:15.394 --> 00:03:18.331
-I did it!

00:03:18.331 --> 00:03:20.767
-Bravo!

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.035
[ Cheering ]

00:03:23.035 --> 00:03:26.005
-Oh, my God, you know, Seth,
it's me and Cardi B.

00:03:26.005 --> 00:03:27.740
We're both
in that little section.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:30.109
-Really?
-Yeah, it's me and Cardi B.

00:03:30.109 --> 00:03:32.245
-Wow, that makes sense.
-That's all I'm saying.

00:03:32.245 --> 00:03:33.780
-You remind me
so much of each other.

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:36.115
-Don't you think?
-Yeah.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:38.017
-When you go to
a giant concert like that

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:41.187
and you see a performer
of Beyonce's magnitude,

00:03:41.187 --> 00:03:43.456
having grown up
as Diana Ross's daughter

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:47.192
and I'm assuming going to shows
like that from a very young age,

00:03:47.192 --> 00:03:49.729
but yet it seems like you
can still be blown away by it.

00:03:49.729 --> 00:03:51.897
-Well, first of all,
I'm a huge fan of Beyonce's,

00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:53.299
love all of her music.

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:54.934
I don't go to a lot of concerts.

00:03:54.934 --> 00:03:56.002
-That's what I was wondering.

00:03:56.002 --> 00:03:58.204
-And I was very overwhelmed.

00:03:58.204 --> 00:04:01.040
So because I'm my mom's child,
I, growing up,

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:03.176
being in a stadium,
I knew the set list,

00:04:03.176 --> 00:04:04.711
so I knew when
the last song was,

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:05.878
when I was going to cut out.

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.380
It was I knew
where I was cutting out.

00:04:07.380 --> 00:04:10.015
I was going backstage,
like, I wasn't just --

00:04:10.015 --> 00:04:12.618
We got to that stadium
with my friends,

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:14.887
and I was like, "I don't know.

00:04:14.887 --> 00:04:16.322
I don't think I can do this."

00:04:16.322 --> 00:04:19.492
They're like, "You got this."
I was like, "I don't know."

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.560
I was like,
there's people everywhere!

00:04:21.560 --> 00:04:23.529
Like, everywhere!

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:25.231
And so we did it,

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.999
and then I was standing
next to Jay-Z,

00:04:26.999 --> 00:04:28.000
so when they started leaving,
I was like,

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.001
"Guys, we got to go now!"

00:04:29.001 --> 00:04:30.069
-Yeah.
-"Jay-Z is leaving.

00:04:30.069 --> 00:04:31.203
We got to go."

00:04:31.203 --> 00:04:32.672
-Probably pretty smart.
-Yeah.

00:04:32.672 --> 00:04:34.073
-And you got out
and everything was good?

00:04:34.073 --> 00:04:35.308
-I got out,
and now I'm in the movie.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:36.375
-Now you're in the movie.
-So worth it.

00:04:36.375 --> 00:04:38.177
I dressed up like a ball.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:40.213
What do you call it?
-A disco ball?

00:04:40.213 --> 00:04:41.781
-I dressed up like a disco ball.

00:04:41.781 --> 00:04:42.882
-I'm so happy that is what --

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.116
Like, if I had said disco ball

00:04:44.116 --> 00:04:45.217
and it was something else,
you're like, "What?"

00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:46.652
-No, it was --

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:49.389
"What did you say
I dressed as?"

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:52.591
-Seth, it wasn't a disco ball,
okay?

00:04:52.591 --> 00:04:53.659
Yeah, like a disco ball.

00:04:53.659 --> 00:04:55.294
-I am so happy
that you came back.

00:04:55.294 --> 00:04:56.462
-I'm so glad to see you.
-It is the best to see you.

00:04:56.462 --> 00:04:59.064
-You guys,
this is Tracee Ellis Ross.

00:04:59.064 --> 00:05:01.634
-"Candy Cane Lane" is
streaming now on Prime Video,

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:03.769
and "American Fiction"
opens in select theaters

00:05:03.769 --> 00:05:05.371
December 15th.

00:05:05.371 --> 00:05:07.540
We're right back
with Mike Birbiglia, everybody!

